WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.420 --> 00:00:16.500
Hi, welcome back to the Wheel of Life
online retreat. This fourth session

00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:27.269
is going to be a meditation. We're going to
use the seven preliminary practices for

00:00:27.269 --> 00:00:37.559
meditation that we learned in the second
segment, and we're going try to have what

00:00:37.559 --> 00:00:55.170
we call a nam chi (NAM 'CHI). nam chi means: can we
recreate the experience of dying in

00:00:55.170 --> 00:01:08.670
meditation? Can we try to recreate
what it's going to feel like as we die? And

00:01:08.670 --> 00:01:17.970
then can we create new pathways in our
mind that are going to kick in ... they're

00:01:17.970 --> 00:01:28.140
going to affect how we die. And we're going to
do a meditation that my teacher asked me

00:01:28.140 --> 00:01:40.770
to do every night. So, of course we do our
coffee meditation at night, just as we're

00:01:40.770 --> 00:01:48.840
falling to sleep, but there is a
tradition to practice dying as we fall

00:01:48.840 --> 00:01:54.210
asleep--because falling asleep is also a
kind of a loss of our rough

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:56.840
consciousness.

00:02:04.550 --> 00:02:16.140
So, let's start our practice dying
meditation. And the picture I chose for

00:02:16.140 --> 00:02:29.850
this meditation is a guy, he's trying
to cut the wire of a bomb. And that's

00:02:29.850 --> 00:02:37.920
what we want to do also. We don't want
one of our old bad seeds--doesn't

00:02:37.920 --> 00:02:42.420
matter which priority--we don't want any
of them to blow up in the moment that we

00:02:42.420 --> 00:02:54.840
die. We talked about four kinds of bad
seeds

00:02:54.840 --> 00:03:06.150
fighting with each other--which one's
going to open first? But we're going to use

00:03:06.150 --> 00:03:18.989
the daily practice of dying as we go to
sleep to get used to calling up a good

00:03:18.989 --> 00:03:24.980
seed as our consciousness drifts
off.

00:03:32.150 --> 00:03:36.230
Okay, so here we go. Let's meditate.

00:03:37.670 --> 00:03:53.519
Sit up straight. The lower
abdomen is slightly pulled in. You do

00:03:53.519 --> 00:04:04.110
that by exhaling extra when you come
to the end of your breath. Little bit of

00:04:04.110 --> 00:04:16.440
a smile. Even though your eyelids are
closed, if you gaze a little bit up ...

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:25.080
slightly, slightly up--not much. As if you
were looking at the sun setting or

00:04:25.080 --> 00:04:43.080
something. That will help you stay more
bright during your meditation. Okay, here

00:04:43.080 --> 00:04:57.479
we go. Let's take ten deep breaths. Deep
exhales. Extra air going out at the end

00:04:57.479 --> 00:05:00.080
of the exhale.

00:05:02.120 --> 00:05:07.550
Don't worry about the inhale, he will
take care of himself.

00:05:09.290 --> 00:05:15.620
Here we go. Start number one with the
exhale.

00:06:23.240 --> 00:06:29.120
First of the seven preliminary steps:
please invite one of your teachers to

00:06:29.120 --> 00:06:31.960
come and sit with you.

00:07:40.430 --> 00:07:50.600
Now think about something you really
loved about this teacher. Some quality

00:07:50.600 --> 00:07:59.860
about them that you really love. This is
also part of the first step, which is

00:07:59.860 --> 00:08:03.310
honoring this teacher.

00:09:06.610 --> 00:09:20.290
That also covers the second step: what
makes our teacher most happy--the biggest

00:09:20.290 --> 00:09:31.660
gift we can make our teacher is to do
good deeds. And just thinking about the

00:09:31.660 --> 00:09:36.600
very high good qualities of our teacher

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:48.850
is one of the best good karmas we can
make. And when we make good karmas for

00:09:48.850 --> 00:10:03.430
ourselves, that's the greatest gift we
can give to our teacher. So, appreciate

00:10:03.430 --> 00:10:11.519
something about your teacher as a gift.

00:10:56.220 --> 00:11:01.829
Now think of some negative seed you
planted in the last 24 hours and regret

00:11:01.829 --> 00:11:09.079
it, and make some commitment to try not
to do it in the next 24 hours.

00:12:01.180 --> 00:12:06.970
Now, equal time, equal attention, great
appreciation for something nice you've

00:12:06.970 --> 00:12:10.200
done in the last 24 hours.

00:13:05.070 --> 00:13:09.590
Then ask your teacher to continue
teaching you.

00:13:56.860 --> 00:14:09.130
Then ask your teacher to stay in your
life. Again, I like to spend about ten

00:14:09.130 --> 00:14:12.080
breaths on each of these steps. Sometimes twenty breaths if I want to enjoy

00:14:13.240 --> 00:14:15.870
them longer.

00:15:13.770 --> 00:15:17.930
Now we'll start the actual meditation.

00:15:19.340 --> 00:15:27.060
Again, that seventh preliminary step
actually comes after the meditation. So,

00:15:27.060 --> 00:15:41.910
after the meditation we'll do the
dedication. Let's go through those four

00:15:41.910 --> 00:15:55.310
priorities of our seeds that's going to
be triggered at the last moment of our

00:15:55.310 --> 00:16:15.810
gross consciousness during death. Our
awareness of this world, this life, it

00:16:15.810 --> 00:16:26.580
will end, and then our awareness will go
back to some very primitive basic

00:16:26.580 --> 00:16:31.760
awareness that we've always had in our
many lifetimes.

00:16:39.530 --> 00:16:50.280
We talked about the bad seeds before, but
now in this meditation, and for the rest

00:16:50.280 --> 00:17:01.880
of your life, when you go to sleep you
can do this meditation. Number one:

00:17:01.880 --> 00:17:05.270
first-in/first-out.

00:17:06.110 --> 00:17:20.220
What was a very early good
karma I can remember doing? Maybe I was a

00:17:20.220 --> 00:17:30.090
little kid in the school, maybe I helped
another child in the school to do their

00:17:30.090 --> 00:17:33.140
homework or something.

00:17:34.730 --> 00:17:47.130
What's an early good karma in my life
that I can still remember? Normally, that

00:17:47.130 --> 00:17:57.900
one will open first as I die, so
please go ahead and think of something

00:17:57.900 --> 00:18:02.810
sweet you did. Even a small thing as a
small child.

00:19:24.039 --> 00:19:35.899
Now normally that seed, because it was
first in, would be first out. So, you could

00:19:35.899 --> 00:19:48.049
expect it perhaps to open early as
you die, but maybe there's other seeds

00:19:48.049 --> 00:19:52.360
that you planted later in your life--

00:19:55.299 --> 00:20:08.840
maybe in your twenties. Good actions that
you repeated over and over. Maybe you

00:20:08.840 --> 00:20:13.269
were a volunteer for some kind of charity,

00:20:14.470 --> 00:20:30.230
and maybe one day a week for a year,
you donated your time. So that good

00:20:30.230 --> 00:20:35.330
seed is going to push back the other one,
and it's going to be the seed that opens

00:20:35.330 --> 00:20:38.259
as you die.

00:21:02.980 --> 00:21:07.990
Imagine dying and this seed opening.

00:21:15.670 --> 00:21:21.570
Again, dying is not losing all
consciousness; it's the the end of the

00:21:21.570 --> 00:21:26.680
gross [@opposite of subtle] awareness of this life, and then
suddenly you're just back to a very

00:21:26.680 --> 00:21:31.380
basic, almost animal, awareness.

00:21:58.330 --> 00:22:03.430
Try to imagine where that habitual good seed--maybe work for a charity--

00:22:03.430 --> 00:22:07.540
what kind of lifetime would it project

00:22:07.540 --> 00:22:31.440
for you? What kind of lifetime might
it create? Maybe a very happy life where

00:22:31.440 --> 00:22:35.550
people are always helping you.

00:23:28.360 --> 00:23:32.970
Now, the next one we can only imagine.

00:23:35.429 --> 00:23:47.080
Suppose we are actually in the hospital,
we are dying--again, which just means that

00:23:47.080 --> 00:23:52.779
the awareness is going to drop from a
detailed awareness of this life to sort

00:23:52.779 --> 00:24:17.470
of a very basic primitive awareness--and
suppose that a relative of ours just

00:24:17.470 --> 00:24:24.750
runs their hand down our arm with a lot
of love. Just lightly they brush our arm

00:24:24.750 --> 00:24:40.090
with love. They run their hand down their
arm. And that touch on my arm reminds me

00:24:40.090 --> 00:24:49.059
of years ago a friend of mine--maybe
someone they loved--died and then I went

00:24:49.059 --> 00:24:56.039
to their house and I was running my hand
down their arm to comfort them.

00:25:09.690 --> 00:25:18.250
And so at the most crucial moment of my
life, as my rough mind stops,

00:25:18.250 --> 00:25:36.850
I remember something kind and
considerate I did many years ago. And

00:25:36.850 --> 00:25:44.650
that seed inserts itself at that moment
between the end of this life and going

00:25:44.650 --> 00:25:49.770
back to my very basic state of mind.

00:26:00.149 --> 00:26:14.679
That memory of serving someone at the
crucial moment of my death, it's going to

00:26:14.679 --> 00:26:19.349
create a very beautiful future life.

00:27:06.149 --> 00:27:13.559
Now, suppose instead that in those last
moments of this life

00:27:13.559 --> 00:27:24.589
I remembered the very, very best good
karma I ever did in my whole life.

00:27:27.889 --> 00:27:32.479
Maybe I saved someone's life.

00:27:34.819 --> 00:27:51.059
Maybe I gave a lot of my money to
someone who needed it. Try to remember ...

00:27:51.059 --> 00:28:03.839
and we're going to spend more time here. Try
to remember the very, very best karma you

00:28:03.839 --> 00:28:07.639
ever planted in your whole life.

00:29:08.690 --> 00:29:15.170
Now imagine that your new life is
beginning from this very, very powerful

00:29:15.170 --> 00:29:29.480
good seed. If that whole
life is defined by that one incredible

00:29:29.480 --> 00:29:33.220
good seed, what would that life be like?

00:30:30.330 --> 00:30:38.660
We've finished the meditation. It's time
to do the seventh and final meditation

00:30:38.660 --> 00:30:49.500
preliminary, which is actually not a
preliminary because it comes after the

00:30:49.500 --> 00:31:01.560
meditation. But, just thinking about all
those good seeds fighting for first

00:31:01.560 --> 00:31:17.850
position in our death, we made a lot of
good seeds just by thinking about our

00:31:17.850 --> 00:31:37.430
good seeds. So, let's give those seeds
away as golden light. Three long, happy

00:31:37.430 --> 00:31:43.250
exhales... the golden light... sharing those
seeds with the whole world.

00:32:01.100 --> 00:32:13.610
And then slowly open your eyes. Take a good
stretch. And we'll see you for session

00:32:13.610 --> 00:32:21.730
five of our lam rim Wheel of Life. Thank you.

